  "worked_solution": "To calculate $g(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ into the expression for $g(x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(2) & =8\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{72}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
